<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">David Komnenos</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1184–<a href="/years/1212">1212</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/david">David</a> Komnenos was a grandson of the Byzantine emperor Andronikos I who, with his brother Alexios, seized <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/trabzon">Trebizond</a> in April 1204 with Georgian troops provided by their kinswoman <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tamar-of-georgia">Queen Tamar</a>. While Alexios ruled as the first emperor of Trebizond, David led campaigns westward along the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/black-sea">Black Sea</a> coast into Paphlagonia but lost ground to the Empire of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nicaea">Nicaea</a>. He died as a monk in 1212.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/david-komnenos.jpg" alt="David Komnenos" width="320" height="165" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Dumbarton Oaks · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Seal_of_David_Komnenos.webp" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
